# Everything `scripts/staging.mjs` generates. None of it is source, all of it is
# either credential material or a per-machine build record, and a nested
# .gitignore is used rather than an entry in the repository root's so that the
# rule lives next to the files it is about.
#
#   tls/                    a local CA, its key, the staging leaf and the leaf's key
#   .env.staging            the session secret, the database password, the image digests
#   release-manifest.json   which image digests this machine built, and from what
#   staging-verified.json   which digests a verified staging run attested to
#   observability/metrics-token
#                           the bearer token Prometheus scrapes /metrics with,
#                           written by scripts/alert-delivery.mjs from
#                           PRL_STAGING_METRICS_TOKEN because compose does not
#                           interpolate the files it mounts
#
# Committing any of them would put a private key in the repository (tls/), a
# secret in the repository (.env.staging), or a machine-local record that changes
# on every build into every diff (the two JSON files). The two JSON files are also
# the reason a committed one would be actively harmful rather than merely noisy:
# `staging promote` trusts staging-verified.json, so a committed one would let a
# promotion inherit somebody else's machine's verdict.
tls/
.env.staging
release-manifest.json
staging-verified.json
observability/metrics-token
